def flatten(d, parent_key='', sep='.'):
    items = []
    for k, v in d.items():
        new_key = f"{parent_key}{sep}{k}" if parent_key else k
        if isinstance(v, dict):
            items.extend(flatten(v, new_key, sep=sep).items())
        elif isinstance(v, list):
            items.extend((f"{new_key}[{i}]": val for i, val in enumerate(v))).items()
        else:
            items.append((new_key, v))
    return dict(items)
```

This function `flatten` takes a nested dictionary `d` and flattens it into a single-level dictionary where the keys are joined with a specified separator (default is `.`). It handles nested dictionaries, lists, and non-dict values as specified.

